Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: stop the iw-extension noise and the empty-variable compares

A bind-mount A/B run on the router (v87-2 image, one "wifi down/up" cycle
each) counted what is still in the log with 0026 applied:

  out of range 39, missing ] 3, iw usage 3, Invalid argument 3,
  json_select warnings 6 ("data" 3 + the "config" cascade, 3)

The sources were traced with `set -x` down to the exact command, and are
fixed here.  Every test that compared an unset variable numerically keeps
its current "not configured, so false" result; only the diagnostics go.

mac80211.sh:

1. mac80211_get_band_name() parses `iw <phy> info` for
   "Idx <n>:" / "Frequency Range:" lines.  That is QSDK iw output; the
   feeds/base iw 6.9 shipped here never prints those lines, so freq1 and
   freq2 stay empty and the 13 range tests below become
   `[ "" -gt 2300 ]` -> "sh: out of range".  Default both ends to 0;
   the function still ends in band_name=invalid, as before, minus the
   noise.  (get_sta_freq_list() has the same parse but feeds awk, which
   does not complain about empty values; leave it alone.)

2. mac80211_setup_monitor() has `[ -n "$channel"]` (no space before the
   closing bracket): "missing ]", and the elif never fired.

3. mac80211_set_vif_txpower() drives two QSDK iw extensions.  ath12k
   rejects every per-VAP txpower form with EINVAL here (`auto`, `fixed`
   and `limit`, with the interface up), and `-l <link_id>` is not known
   to stock iw at all.  iw prints its usage text on stdout, so the
   `2>/dev/null` that 0026 put on set_intf_offload did not silence it.
   Redirect both streams on the txpower calls and on set_intf_offload;
   the calls stay in place for a driver/iw combination that can use
   them.

4. mac80211_set_fq_limit() starts with an unconditional
   `json_select data`.  With no data section this prints
   "Variable 'data' does not exist", and the following `json_select ..`
   pops past the root, so the next `json_select config` warns as well.
   Probe with the warning redirected instead.

5. The same warning comes from the `json_select data && { ... }` in
   drv_mac80211_setup(): json_select prints it before the && can stop
   the block.  Redirect the probe.

6. `[ "$ml_max_rec_links" -ge 0 ]`, `[ "$min_tx_power" -gt 0 ]`,
   `[ "$wds" -gt 0 ] || [ "$wds_ie" -gt 0 ]`, `[ "$wds_ie" -gt 0 ]` and
   the two 6 GHz FILS tests all run on options that are unset on a stock
   config.  Default them to 0 inside the test.  For ml_max_rec_links the
   variable is simply required to be set, because defaulting it to 0
   would append "ml_max_rec_links=0" to hostapd.conf.

7. The 5 GHz radar block reads
   `json_get_vars background_radar:0 bgcac_en:0 dfs_bw_reduce_en:0
   rcac_freq:0 interCACChan` -- interCACChan is the only one without a
   ":0" default, so `[ "$interCACChan" -gt 0 ]` compared an empty value
   on every 5 GHz BSS.

hostapd.sh (same package):

8. `[ "$multi_ap_vlanid" -gt 0 -a "$multi_ap_vlanid" -le 4094 ]`: unset
   unless a VLAN is configured.  Require it to be set first.

9. `[ "$mbo" -eq 1 ]` on three lines: empty when mbo is not configured.
   Require it to be set first.

10. dpp and eppk are only set for DPP/EPPKE configs, but three sites
    compare them numerically: two in hostapd_append_wpa_key_mgmt() (DPP,
    EPPKE), one right after the config_id append, and one in the
    wpa_supplicant network_data builder.  Default both to 0 in the test.

11. `[ -n "$vlan_possible"]`: same missing-bracket bug as the monitor
    line; "missing ]" per BSS.

Before/after on the traced cycle: out of range 39 -> 0, missing ] 3 -> 0,
iw usage 3 -> 0, Invalid argument 3 -> 0, json_select warnings 6 -> 0.

